silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_02_twelve_leg_deep_dive_sections_12_taxonomy_leg_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'TaxonomyLegConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, FelisCatusTSN183798: the ITIS database entry for Felis catus, TSN 183798, Kingdom Animalia, Phylum Chordata, Class Mammalia, Order Carnivora, Family Felidae, Genus Felis, Species catus; accessible at cannon/tax/ITIS.sqlite; also, TaxonomyArrow_ITIS: the typed arrow FelisCatusTSN183798 -> MittensColimitApex; distinct from classification_leg (DomesticCat -> MittensColimitApex); also, ITISSqliteDatabase: the local ITIS taxonomy database at cannon/tax/ITIS.sqlite; the source cannon witness for FelisCatusTSN183798." .
